axis are pointing toward the origin, meaning that the solutions of the form \n${c}_{2}{e}^{{\\lambda }_{2}t}[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]$\nmust approach the origin as $t\\to \\infty .$ So, we must have ${\\lambda }_{2}<0.$\n\nAmong the options, the only system that satisfies ${\\lambda }_{1}>0$ and ${\\lambda }_{2}<0$ is the following:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}{x}^{′}(t)=4x(t) \\\\ {y}^{′}(t)=-y(t)\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-332692/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "d81d981f-ab55-5637-bff5-ae47633b0b79"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-332692"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} [:db/retract 17592186167155 :question/answer-fields 17592186164317] {:db/id "q-332717/selection/ma-v1/55d445ed7ca30f236ca7dfa23f28cf1dfbbf69d0a305613a958e3bdc1f1e6699/71e848120bf6e055d09bfbf6736a71c82d9c7fe06bd5ef3a927aea504efbd3fd" :answer/id #uuid "b5b286bd-e364-5c90-a31e-71b9969c19b3" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{\\begin{aligned}{x}^{′}(t)=5x(t) \\\\ {y}^{′}(t)=-2y(t)\\end{aligned}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-332717/selection/ma-v1/55d445ed7ca30f236ca7dfa23f28cf1dfbbf69d0a305613a958e3bdc1f1e6699/2a63a57b890157b91053d0c5d6028b72b938b85994472af20d85b57adbadec50" :answer/id #uuid "34967850-d3e5-5fd4-a467-eef1387bdfe4" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{\\begin{aligned}{x}^{′}(t)=-2x(t) \\\\ {y}^{′}(t)=-5y(t)\\end{aligned}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-332717/selection/ma-v1/55d445ed7ca30f236ca7dfa23f28cf1dfbbf69d0a305613a958e3bdc1f1e6699/761ca41454cf386491acdc3fc2ee895be91d4e3f5dcac1c2b553f30766ff20e5" :answer/id #uuid "aa8d281d-68f6-577c-a8ad-498ed4315ec0" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{\\begin{aligned}{x}^{′}(t)=2x(t) \\\\ {y}^{′}(t)=5y(t)\\end{aligned}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-332717/selection/ma-v1/55d445ed7ca30f236ca7dfa23f28cf1dfbbf69d0a305613a958e3bdc1f1e6699/847a8ae78